        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Alfred L. Werker, Del Andrews, Erich von Stroheim, Boots Mallory, ZaSu Pitts, Jon Jost\n- Companies: Fox Film Corporation\n- Works: Ridin' the Wind, Hello, Sister!\n- Roles: film director, independent filmmaker\n\nFacts:\n- Alfred L. Werker was born on December 2, 1896, and he was a film director whose movie career spanned from 1917 through 1957.\n- In 1925, Alfred L. Werker co-directed his first film, \"Ridin' the Wind,\" with director Del Andrews after working in film production jobs and assistant directing.\n- In 1933, Fox Film Corporation executives brought Alfred L. Werker in to re-shoot and re-edit Erich von Stroheim's film \"Hello, Sister!,\" which co-starred Boots Mallory and ZaSu Pitts.\n- Jon Jost was born on 16 May 1943 in Chicago, and he is an American independent filmmaker.",
